schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: 'Case Studies: How Nonprofits Are Using Web3'
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: case-linked
  summary: >-
    Surveys real-world nonprofit adoption of crypto: Ukraine's 2022 emergency
    crypto fundraising after banks froze, Mercy Corps Ventures cutting delivery
    costs 60% with stablecoins in Syria, and the fast growth of crypto
    donations reported by The Giving Block. Frames web3 tools as practical
    infrastructure (fast settlement, transparency, lower cross-border fees)
    rather than a speculative novelty, and gives small nonprofits a low-effort
    on-ramp (accept crypto donations, use stablecoins for cross-border
    payments, use blockchain records for transparent reporting).
  audience: nonprofit staff and small charity operators new to crypto
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      article leans on cited statistics from interested parties (The Giving
      Block, CryptoAltruists) without independent verification
  related_concepts:
    - stablecoins
    - crypto-donations
    - blockchain-transparency
  related_resources:
    - the-giving-block
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/case-studies-nonprofits.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
